  "worked_solution": "Factoring the constant out of the integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(-3\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  & =-3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =-3(-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta )\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =3(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta )\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =3[\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}\u20610] \\\\  & =3(0-1) \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
